Subject: [PATCH] appDisplay: refresh the app info list before the folder views

AppDisplay._redisplay() reloads every folder view before calling
super._redisplay(), and AppDisplay._loadApps() -- reached from there -- is
the only writer of this._appInfoList. FolderView._loadApps() matches its
`categories` key against that same list, through
AppDisplay.getAppInfos(), so a folder view always filters the app list of
the *previous* redisplay.

An application installed while the session is running is therefore claimed
by no folder on the first pass: it is appended to the root grid instead,
and only filed into its folder on the next redisplay -- the next install,
or the next session. Hoist the refresh into its own method and call it at
the top of AppDisplay._redisplay(), before the folder views reload.

_loadApps() has exactly one caller (BaseAppView._redisplay) and is always
reached through the patched method, and both fields the filter reads are
set in the BaseAppView constructor, so the earlier call is safe.

Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-shell (still present on main)
--- a/js/ui/appDisplay.js
+++ b/js/ui/appDisplay.js
@@ -1375,6 +1375,15 @@
     }
 
     _redisplay() {
+        // FolderView._loadApps() matches its `categories` against
+        // AppDisplay.getAppInfos(), so the installed-app list has to be
+        // refreshed before the folder views reload. Refreshing it below, in
+        // super._redisplay() -> _loadApps(), is one pass too late: a freshly
+        // installed application is matched against the previous pass's list,
+        // so no folder claims it and it lands on the root grid until the next
+        // redisplay.
+        this._refreshAppInfoList();
+
         this._folderIcons.forEach(icon => {
             icon.view._redisplay();
         });
@@ -1487,8 +1496,7 @@
         return aPosition - bPosition;
     }
 
-    _loadApps() {
-        const appIcons = [];
+    _refreshAppInfoList() {
         this._appInfoList = Shell.AppSystem.get_default().get_installed().filter(appInfo => {
             try {
                 appInfo.get_id(); // catch invalid file encodings
@@ -1498,6 +1506,10 @@
             return !this._appFavorites.isFavorite(appInfo.get_id()) &&
                 this._parentalControlsManager.shouldShowApp(appInfo);
         });
+    }
+
+    _loadApps() {
+        const appIcons = [];
 
         const apps = this._appInfoList.map(app => app.get_id());
 
